{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[dict(id='M-bootstrap-contract',file='api.go',start_line=227,end_line=238,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-helper-bootstrap',file='testing.go',start_line=812,end_line=825,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-inmem-rpc',file='inmem_transport.go',start_line=103,end_line=201,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-inmem-init',file='inmem_transport.go',start_line=53,end_line=80,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-shutdown',file='api.go',start_line=1010,end_line=1026,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-shutdown-future',file='future.go',start_line=166,end_line=180,kind='code_observation')]\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='revision_needed',source_ids=['M-bootstrap-contract','M-helper-bootstrap','M-bootstrap','M-start','M-elect-producer','M-election','M-inmem-rpc','M-inmem-init','M-verify-register','M-verify-vote','M-notify','M-consume','M-suffrage-contract','M-api-verify','M-shutdown','M-shutdown-future'],challenged_components=['initialization'],rationale='Fixed artifact 9d973332dc8541c0a2b2963b3c3ed0b4 was inspected with its executed source and plan, Claim C-verify-eligible v1 and raw CheckRun ea5cefa3de614a53a6e123037b005004. Prepared/admitted/result correlate by independent operation verify-1. The result has completed=true, success=true, eligible_voter_support=1, quorum=2, positive_append_responses={n:1}, state Leader term 2. The success=>eligible quorum implication is encoded correctly, not as equivalence. Wrapper counters are mutex protected and increment before returning successful RPCs; all voter append paths are blocked from before replication starts, pipelines are disabled, and no snapshots exist to supply alternate voter support. Therefore absence of positive voter responses is stronger than the per-request absence needed. Empty blocked_calls in this execution means those workers had not reached a blocked call, not that voter support was observed or assumed. One nonvoter callback is sufficient through the inspected register/vote/result path. The contract inference concerns voter eligibility in a voter-threshold authority confirmation, not proof the elected leader was already obsolete. The material unresolved problem is initial history: the fixed harness calls BootstrapCluster on all three voters and the nonvoter, whereas M-bootstrap-contract says the cluster can only be bootstrapped once from a single participating voter. M-helper-bootstrap demonstrates repository tests using repeated identical per-node bootstrap, so the discrepancy is not proof of an illegal history; however it does not resolve the public caller duty for this fixed driver. Repair only initialization by bootstrapping the elected voter and letting other empty constructor-created nodes participate through real RPC handlers; preserve membership, election, pre-replication failure policy and the oracle. NewRaft permits empty stores and requestVote explicitly handles empty peer lists, so this has a sourced route rather than inventing histories. This review does not clear correspondence pending that repair and fresh execution.',counterevidence=['Repository testing.go bootstraps each peer with identical configuration, supporting the current shape but conflicting with the API single-participating-voter wording.','Lease protection remains enabled and could reject later; current measurement completes before its first 5-second check.','The candidate is made ready directly by the harness; no timeout expiry was observed. Its voter/no-known-leader entry preconditions and actual persisted voting are present.'],limitations=['No second leader or stale FSM read was exercised.','The initial current-term noop is not committed; the public verification procedure has no current-term-commit prerequisite, but this is not an application read-safety test.','Follower election/snapshot/FSM workers are not scheduled in th